==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|la|acroamaticus}}, {{m|la|acroaticus||esoteric}}, originally in reference to the esoteric oral teachings of {{w|Aristotle}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἀκροαματικός||for hearing only; esoteric}}, from {{m|grc|ἀκροάομαι||to listen}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[esoteric|Esoteric]], [[abstruse]]; {{lb|en|in particular}} pertaining to [[teaching]]s that are taught [[orally]] and not [[write down|written down]] for a wider public.
# Of or [[related]] to [[lecture]]s.
